# L1 Architecture

## Layers
- `Infrastructure` — DI, entry point, scene bootstrap
- `Gameplay` / `Meta` — feature logic and scene contexts
- `UI` — Views (MonoBehaviour) + Presenters (plain C#)
- `Configs` — ScriptableObjects; load via `ConfigsProviderService` / `ResourcesConfigsLoader`
- `Utilities` — shared services (assets, input, scenes, data)

## DI
- Custom `DIContainer`: project scope + scene scope
- Register in `*ContextRegistrations`; resolve via factories/services
- Scene container disposed on switch (`SceneSwitcherService`) — implement `IDisposable` for pooled/DDOL services
- Do not service-locate via `FindObjectOfType` in feature code (bootstrap exception only)

## Composition root
- Scene `*Bootstrap` : `SceneBootstrap` — registrations, `Initialize`, `Run`, and frame `Update`/`LateUpdate` Tick
- Create gameplay objects through factories (`CharactersFactory`, `WeaponFactory`, …), not ad-hoc `Instantiate` + wiring in random scripts

## Logic vs Unity
- Prefer plain C# classes with `Tick(float dt)` (`PlayerMotor`, `PlayerWeaponVisualFollow`, services)
- MonoBehaviour only when Unity requires it: scene hooks, SerializeField refs, physics messages, animation events
- Owner MB (e.g. `Player`, `PlayerCamera`, bootstrap) calls Tick — do not put gameplay state machines inside `Update` on many components
- Never use `DefaultExecutionOrder`
